/*
  core/masks/fearful_authorize.spthy -- f_H for the NEW Fearful mask, AUTHORIZE action.
  (Plan §3: the low-trust user who withdraws from anything security-critical.)

  Fearful ABORTS the authorization -- it refuses to proceed even when the request is legitimate
  (Whitten & Tygar "unmotivated"/distrust; outcome abort()/withdrawal). It produces NO !AuthDone,
  so the ceremony safely STALLS at this step (safe-fail, distinct from Careless's passive timeout:
  this is an *active* refusal). RespMask(P,'Fearful') is gated by the current-mask restrictions:
  Fearful must be the current mask (set by sigma5 SecurityAnxiety).
*/

rule Authorize_Fearful_abort:
    [ !AuthReq(P, aid) ]
  --[ Authorize(P, aid, 'Fearful'), RespMask(P,'Fearful'), Abort(P, aid), Answered(aid) ]->
    [ ]
